  "vulnerability_information": "**Description:**\nIf a `Set-Cookie` header contains an `=` immediately after a semicolon (i.e., `;=`), curl stops parsing the attributes and discards everything that follows. This silently drops protections like `Secure` and `HttpOnly`, causing curl to later send the cookie over unencrypted HTTP.\n\n**Root Cause:**\nIn `parse_cookie_header()` (`lib/cookie.c:614`), an `=` immediately following a `;` causes `curlx_str_cspn` to fail with a zero-length match. This terminates the attribute-parsing loop early, before the `Secure` attribute is ever evaluated.\n\n**Impact:**\nSensitive cookie data is sent in plaintext over the network (CWE-201).\n\n**Steps to Reproduce (PoC):**\n\n1. Start a local HTTPS server with a self-signed certificate for the name\n   `cookie.test`, and a plain-HTTP server on a second port. The HTTPS one\n   returns this header:\n\n   Set-Cookie: session=secret;=x; Secure\n\n2. Fetch the HTTPS URL with curl 8.22.0 and save the cookie jar. `--resolve`\n   points the name at the local server, so no DNS and no public host are\n   needed; `-k` is only for the self-signed certificate:\n\n   curl -k -c jar.txt --resolve cookie.test:8443:127.0.0.1 https://cookie.test:8443/\n\n3. Inspect `jar.txt`. The fourth tab-separated field is the Secure flag:\n\n   cookie.test\tFALSE\t/\tFALSE\t0\tsession\tsecret\n\n4. Request the same host name over plaintext HTTP, reusing the jar:\n\n   curl -b jar.txt --resolve cookie.test:8080:127.0.0.1 http://cookie.test:8080/\n\nExpected Result:\nThe `Secure` attribute is applied, so field 4 of the jar reads TRUE and the\nplaintext request in step 4 carries no `Cookie:` header.\n\nActual Result:\nField 4 reads FALSE and the plaintext server receives the cookie:\n\n   GET / HTTP/1.1\n   Host: cookie.test:8080\n   User-Agent: curl/8.22.0\n   Accept: */*\n   Cookie: session=secret\n\nParsing was truncated at the `;=` sequence, so `Secure` was never evaluated.\n\n**Reproduction script:**\none command\n\n```bash\npython  poc.py\n```\n{F6928292}\n\n{F6928297}\n\n{F6928301}\n\n## Impact\n\n-",
